<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Habibullah Kalakani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1891">1891</a>–<a href="/years/1929">1929</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bacha-i Saqao, Habibullah Ghazi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Habibullah Kalakani, nicknamed Bacha-i Saqao ('son of the water carrier'), was a Tajik rebel from the Shomali plain north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a>. Exploiting the revolts against King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amanullah-khan">Amanullah Khan</a>'s reforms, he seized Kabul in January 1929 and ruled as emir for nine months. Nadir Khan's forces took Kabul in October 1929, and Habibullah was executed in November.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/habibullah-kalakani.jpg" alt="Habibullah Kalakani" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Habibull%C4%81h_Kalak%C4%81ni_Portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
